{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>Whom Moses and Aaron counted.</b> Pointed with a dot on the וְאַהֲרֹן, to say that he was not in the counting of the Levites (Bekhorot 4)." "<b>Two and twenty thousand.</b> But when you sum them individually you find three hundred extra — the sons of Gershon: seven thousand and five hundred; the sons of Kohath: eight thousand and six hundred; the sons of Merari: six thousand and two hundred. And why were they not included with the rest, so that they would redeem the firstborn and the two hundred and seventy-three firstborn remaining over the counting would not need redemption? Our Sages said in tractate Bekhorot (page 5): those three hundred Levites were themselves firstborn, and it is sufficient that they exempt themselves from redemption."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:17.787424664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}